  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I am writing as a long-time VRChat user to share some feedback regarding the current world (map) favorites system. At the moment, users are limited to four world favorite folders with a total cap of 400 worlds. While this may have been sufficient in the past, I feel that for today’s VRChat—where the number, quality, and diversity of worlds continue to grow rapidly—this limitation has become increasingly restrictive.\n\nMany players, myself included, enjoy exploring and collecting a wide variety of worlds for different purposes, such as social events, exploration, roleplay, photography, or personal memories. Because of the current cap, we are often forced to delete older favorite worlds in order to save new ones. This can feel frustrating, especially when those older worlds hold sentimental value or are still meaningful but cannot be revisited frequently. Having to constantly “choose what to forget” negatively impacts the overall user experience.\n\nI would like to kindly suggest expanding the number of world favorite folders, in a similar way to how avatar favorite folders have been increased in the past. For example, increasing the default number of world favorite folders from 4 to 8 would already make a significant difference for many users. Additionally, offering even more world favorite folders as a benefit for VRChat Plus members would likely be very well received by the community and add further value to the membership.\n\nI believe this change would greatly improve world management, encourage exploration, and make it easier for users to engage with the ever-growing creative content in VRChat. Many players would truly appreciate this improvement.",
